Green phase for the Conductor review of native_scene_integration_20260925.
Applies every High, Medium, and Low finding raised in review.

Correctness
- Declared resources are duplicated per attempt, so a retry no longer
  inherits a resource a previous attempt mutated and retained. The shipped
  retry E2E passed only because nothing retained the reference; a probe that
  retained it in suite state proved the leak, and the new E2E pins the fix.
- Screenshot capture keeps the original failure message and appends the
  capture error, instead of replacing it and turning exit 1 into a bare
  exit 2. A cleanup failure now reports the assertion that failed first
  alongside the cleanup error.
- Each failing windowed test writes its own capture, so several failures in
  one suite no longer overwrite each other.
- A retention failure republishes the index with status error, so the
  recorded status can no longer disagree with the exit code.
- find_nodes matches a name substring, so the documented 'Target*' example
  works and an empty or invalid pattern reports integration_node_pattern
  instead of silently matching nothing.
- A test method with parameters is no longer treated as a runnable test, so
  an INTEGRATION override targeting it is reported instead of silently
  validating for a test that never runs.
- Bounded preflight process output, so a chatty engine cannot flood the CLI
  error or JUnit. Exit code is unchanged.

Artifacts
- The index lists only artifacts that exist, and 'screenshots' lists only
  realized captures, so it no longer advertises dangling paths.
- Retention removes only directories carrying this tool's run markers, so a
  user directory kept under the artifact root is never deleted.
- The artifact index location is printed in CLI output, so it is
  discoverable without reading JUnit.

Tests
- Added AC6 coverage: a windowed suite on a headless renderer is an
  explicit suite-level error with exit 2 and no test execution.
- Strengthened weak assertions: the scene-load diagnostic now asserts the
  message names the asset and type; missing-lookup diagnostics assert the
  structured kind and identifier instead of a JSON substring; the artifact
  index test asserts real behavior instead of round-tripping a value the
  test itself wrote; the doctor pass test asserts the version it read; the
  TimeoutExpired branch is covered alongside TimeoutError.
- The screenshot write-failure test asserts the structured engine error
  rather than Godot's English text, and uses a guarded lookup.
- The display guard no longer treats a windowed assertion failure as a
  missing display.
- Godot project import retries once: it intermittently exits non-zero after
  a completed filesystem scan under load, which failed an unrelated test in
  two consecutive full runs.

Docs
- find_nodes and get_integration rows corrected; the full context failure
  list added; the parameterized-method rule documented; per-test captures,
  the capture-failure behavior, index discoverability, and real index
  contents documented; the doctor staleness warning and the inert artifact
  step corrected; the stale ROADMAP deferral of scene/resource integration
  removed.

Verification: 1093 unit/integration and 75 E2E tests pass; Ruff, Black,
gdlint, gdformat, and git diff --check clean.

Deferred, disclosed: the ~150 duplicated E2E helper lines across four
modules are still drifted, and two pre-existing tight wall-clock assertions
